menu "Example configuration"

    config EXAMPLE_RE_A_GPIO
        int "GPIO number of the encoder pin A"
        range 0 54
        default 16
        help
            The GPIO connected to the pin A of the encoder. The encoder has no
            direction, so the pins A and B can be swapped, but they must differ.

    config EXAMPLE_RE_B_GPIO
        int "GPIO number of the encoder pin B"
        range 0 54
        default 17
        help
            The GPIO connected to the pin B of the encoder. The pins A and B
            must differ.

    config EXAMPLE_RE_BTN_GPIO
        int "GPIO number of the encoder button"
        range -1 54
        default 18
        help
            The GPIO connected to the push button of the encoder, if any. The
            driver reads the button as active low, so connect the other side of
            the button to ground.

            Set to -1 if the encoder has no button.

endmenu
